.TH DAQ_ALERT 3 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-bigredbox 2.0.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
daq_alert \- Python library for sending Big Red Box alerts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B from daq_alert import send_alert, AlertSender, DEFAULT_PORT, DEFAULT_BROADCAST_IP
.PP
.BI "send_alert(" system_id ", " message ", broadcast_ip=DEFAULT_BROADCAST_IP, port=DEFAULT_PORT) \-> None"
.PP
.BI "sender = AlertSender(broadcast_ip=DEFAULT_BROADCAST_IP, port=DEFAULT_PORT)"
.BI "sender.send(" system_id ", " message ") \-> None"
.fi
.PP
.B DEFAULT_PORT
is 37020;
.B DEFAULT_BROADCAST_IP
is
.BR \(dq255.255.255.255\(dq .
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B daq_alert
package (distribution
.BR daq\-alert ,
version 1.0.0, source
.IR libs/python/daq_alert/ )
sends one alert datagram per call:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
json.dumps({"system_id": system_id,
            "timestamp": datetime.now().isoformat(timespec="seconds"),
            "message": message}).encode("utf\-8")
.fi
.RE
.PP
to
.IR broadcast_ip : port
from a fresh socket with
.B SO_BROADCAST
set.
The encoding is Python's
.B json.dumps
default: a space after
.B ,
and
.BR : ,
non\-ASCII characters as
.BR \euXXXX ,
DEL as
.BR \eu007f .
The timestamp is local time without a zone offset, to the second.
.PP
.B AlertSender
stores the address and port and calls
.B send_alert()
for each
.BR send() .
.PP
The keyword for the destination is
.BR broadcast_ip ,
not
.BR ip .
.PP
The listener package carries a second implementation with the same
signature and the same bytes,
.BR mu2edaq_bigredbox.demo_sender.send_alert ,
whose default port is taken from
.B CRS_PORT_UDP
when that is set; it also prints what it sent.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B OSError
Socket creation or
.B sendto
failed, including
.B EMSGSIZE
for a datagram over 65507 bytes.
.TP
.B socket.gaierror
.I broadcast_ip
is neither an address nor a resolvable host name.
.PP
There is no length limit below the UDP maximum, unlike
.BR libdaq_alert (3),
which rejects fields over 2041 bytes.
.SH NOTES
Install with
.B "pip install libs/python"
or through the CMake install of
.IR libs/ .
.PP
The repository root contains
.IR daq_alert.py ,
a launcher for the listener.
A Python process started with the checkout root as its first path entry
imports that file instead of this package; run sender code from elsewhere.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS 4
.nf
from daq_alert import send_alert, AlertSender

send_alert("DAQ\-NODE\-01", "Readout buffer overflow")

tracker = AlertSender(broadcast_ip="192.0.2.25", port=37020)   # unicast
tracker.send("TRK\-DTC\-03", "link down")
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libdaq_alert (3),
.BR libdaq_alert_cpp (3),
.BR mu2edaq\-bigredbox\-api (7),
.BR mu2edaq\-bigredbox\-send (1),
.BR example\-sender\-py (1)
